### R152 buildHelpReply / badges / On the board
👟 *On the board*
Earned by playing a first game at this club. A game counts once it's finished and the player was in the confirmed squad or on the team sheet.
Once earned, it stays.

Badges are worked out from all finished games at this club.

### R152 buildHelpReply / badges / Regular
🔟 *Regular*
Earned by playing 10 or more games at this club. Every finished game the player was in the confirmed squad or on the team sheet for counts.
Once earned, it stays.

Badges are worked out from all finished games at this club.

### R152 buildHelpReply / badges / Iron Man
🦾 *Iron Man*
Earned when both are true:
1. Played every match at this club since joining. Matches from before they joined don't count against them.
2. At least 3 matches have been played in that time.
It ends with the first missed match, and that match always counts, so it doesn't come back.

Badges are worked out from all finished games at this club.

### R152 buildHelpReply / badges / Man of the Match
🏆 *Man of the Match*
Earned by winning the Man of the Match vote once. If two or more players tie on the most votes, they all win it.
Once earned, it stays.

Badges are worked out from all finished games at this club.

### R152 buildHelpReply / badges / MoM Machine
👑 *MoM Machine*
Earned by winning the Man of the Match vote 3 or more times. A tie on the most votes counts as a win for everyone in the tie.
Once earned, it stays.

Badges are worked out from all finished games at this club.

### R152 buildHelpReply / badges / Masterclass
🌟 *Masterclass*
Earned with one game where the ratings the other players gave average 9 or more. One game is enough.
Once earned, it stays.

Badges are worked out from all finished games at this club.

### R152 buildHelpReply / badges / Mr Reliable
🧱 *Mr Reliable*
Earned when all three are true:
1. Rated in at least 4 games.
2. An average rating of 6.5 or more across all their ratings.
3. Steady from game to game: their game-by-game averages don't swing much. In numbers, the spread (standard deviation) is under 1 point. A player who scores 7, 7.5, 6.8, 7.2 qualifies. One who scores 9, 5, 8, 5.5 doesn't, even if the average is similar.
It can be lost if the ratings drop or start to swing, and comes back when they settle again.

Badges are worked out from all finished games at this club.

### R152 buildHelpReply / badges / Above the Curve
📈 *Above the Curve*
Earned when both are true:
1. Rated in at least 3 games.
2. Their average rating (every rating they've received) is higher than the club average (every rating given to every player in the club's games).
It can be lost if their average drops to the club average or below, and comes back when it climbs above it again.

Badges are worked out from all finished games at this club.

